      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So for the camera, you can take it out of streamer mode. What I do is use the UI attached to the camera preview. Where you select stream mode there is three options. I forget exactly how the first option is labeled, but selecting that will put the desktop window back to first person. The middle option also would do this, but it's multi layer mode.\n\nFor the second part I have no idea where stream mode is in the menu (I'll find it on my own time later), but if you open up the wheel menu and go into the options, one of the options is name plate visibility. One down side with the first person view is whatever you see is what it sees. So you kinda want to hide name tags from yourself",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-18T17:35:25.354Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1st Part:\n\nI wish that using the stream camera (or maybe even mormal camera mode), that it wouldn't immediately make the screen whatever the Camera sees, the application shows. I wish we could choose between the two, like choosing the game screen or what the camera sees as we stream. The suggestion basically is just me asking to make it so whichever camera mode the camera is on, we can choose between the Camera or Game itself to be the output. (Unless there's a already a way to do that- I have zero clue.)\n\n2nd Part:\n\nWhy is it that streaming mode doesn't hide EVERYONE'S name? Shouldn't everyone's name be hidden? (Not mad just the reason for the suggestion) Like it's great that it hides Yours, but when your menu is open, I feel like it should change everyone's name to the same way. (Not including Groups. I feel like just Users) So this 2nd part suggestion is just requesting everyones names be hidden for streamer mode.",
